2026/04/05 17:12:46 [UI] User hit Enter. Sending: "Currently it is very difficult for a person who doesn\\'t ship everyday to create a label. Users who might only ship periodically will benefit from the voice agent. As well as shipping managers looking for a more powerful interface there can be a version for both. The ai agent should be able to handle the quotation and label creation. There should be a traditional form to fall back on and if users prefer. Casual shippers who only ship a few times per year or  travelers who left an item at their hotel, the frontdesk will tell the customer once its found to send them a label,  are ideal users for core app. E-commerce sellers, small shipping room managers, enterprise customers down the road where more powerful interfaces could be developed. Voice should be central for all editions. The voice ui should provide an interface for mobile, tablet or desktop that mirrors the voice conversationally and only allowing input if the user panics or there is an issue. so while the user is giving the voice agent the information, they can watch the data being filled in visually. Conversational voice is the killer concept for these workflows. The elevenlabs conversational ai is perfect for now. It allows integration to and from using webhooks, quote and label information can be sent from elevenlabs conversational ai to the app. Knowledge docs for ups/fedex and usps can be uploaded to elevenlabs rag datbase to allow voice agent to be intelligent about shipping services. for example, all conversations should start with weight of package and to and from zip codes, optional customer can say how fast they want it to ararive, or get multple quotes.  elevenlabs sends that data to our server, where its simulaneously sent to ups, fedex and usps. response back is normalized across the board and the best, fastest, cheapest or requested quotes. for exampe if the customer only gives weight and zip codes, it will give the best option for each shippng speed, so if fedex is cheapest for 1 day/overnight, ups is cheapest for ground etc. 2.3 see above 3.1 need table matching the services for each provider, for example fedex overnight is the same as ups next day 2. special feature like saturday delivery and call tags should be possible in the api, but focus on standard shipping for mvp. Scheduling pick ups is a must. Weight is mandatory, dimensions is optional, but in the case of dimensional weight items invoice will be adjusted at the time of scanning, so user needs to be aware light, large volume parcels should include dimensions. Allow guest checkout. Karrio already has all the connections in a  unifed api so unless there are constraints then opt for karrio for mvp. Domestic only for mvp. Address validation done using karrio api at time of QUOTE and more detailed at time of label creaton. Tracking is a must'"
